2.1.x.x Material List
a. UI Specifications
Material List Screen

Brief Description
This screen displays the list of material records in the system. It allows the authorized actor to view, search, filter, and navigate to material details or the material form for creating or updating material information. This screen supports master data management for raw materials used in product BOM and production planning.

Mockup Screen
[Insert mockup of Material List Screen here]

UI Components / Field Description / Requirements

No.	Component / Field	Type	Description	Requirements / Notes
1	Page Title	Label	Display screen name: Material List	Fixed text
2	Breadcrumb	Label	Show navigation path, e.g. Home > Material Management > Material List	Optional
3	Search Bar	Textbox	Allows user to enter keyword to search materials by code or name	Accept partial match
4	Status Filter	Dropdown	Filter materials by status	Values: All, Active, Inactive
5	Material Type Filter	Dropdown	Filter materials by material category/type	Optional depending on scope
6	Search Button	Button	Execute search/filter action	Refresh result grid
7	Reset Button	Button	Clear search/filter criteria	Return default list
8	Add New Button	Button	Navigate to Material Form Screen for creating new material	Visible only to actor with permission
9	Material Table	Data Grid	Display material list	Supports paging
10	Material Code	Column	Unique code of material	Clickable to open detail
11	Material Name	Column	Name of material	Required display
12	Unit	Column	Unit of measure of material	Example: sheet, kg, meter
13	Standard Size	Column	Standard dimension/specification of material	Optional if applicable
14	Status	Column	Current status of material	Active / Inactive
15	Updated At	Column	Last updated date/time	Format dd/MM/yyyy HH:mm
16	View Detail Action	Icon/Button	Open Material Detail Screen	One row one action
17	Edit Action	Icon/Button	Open Material Form Screen in edit mode	Visible only to actor with permission
18	Pagination	Control	Navigate between pages	Default page size configurable

UI Requirements / Notes

The screen shall display only materials that the actor is authorized to access.
The material list shall be shown in descending order of latest updated record by default.
The user may search by Material Code or Material Name.
Clicking on Material Code or View Detail shall navigate to Material Detail Screen.
Clicking Add New shall navigate to Material Form Screen in create mode.
Clicking Edit shall navigate to Material Form Screen in update mode.
If no data matches the search criteria, the system shall display an empty state with message: with "No material found."
Inactive materials may still appear in the list for traceability, depending on filter condition.
This screen is a list/navigation screen, not a CRUD use case by itself; it may cover multiple use cases such as viewing, searching, and navigating to material detail/form.
b. UC Specifications
UC-MAT-01_View Material List

ID and Name
UC-MAT-01 – View Material List

Primary Actor:
Authorized User

Secondary Actor:
Production Manager, Administrator

Description:
As an authorized user, I want to view the list of materials so that I can monitor and access material master data used in BOM and production activities.

Preconditions:

The actor has logged into the system successfully.
The actor has permission to access material management.

Postconditions:

The material list is displayed on screen.
The actor can continue to search, filter, or open material detail/form.

Normal Flow:

The actor selects Material Management from the navigation menu.
The system opens Material List Screen.
The system retrieves material records from the database.
The system displays the material list with default paging and sorting.
The actor views the displayed material information.

Alternative Flows:

A1. No material data exists

In step 3, the system does not find any material record.
The system displays an empty list with "No material found."

Exception:

E1. Actor has no permission

In step 1, the actor attempts to access the screen without permission.
The system denies access and displays with "You do not have permission to access this function."

Business Rule:

BR-01: Only authorized users can access Material List Screen.
BR-02: Material code must be unique in the system.
BR-03: Inactive materials may still be displayed for historical reference.
UC-MAT-02_Search Material

ID and Name
UC-MAT-02 – Search Material

Primary Actor:
Authorized User

Secondary Actor:
Production Manager, Administrator

Description:
As an authorized user, I want to search and filter materials so that I can quickly find the required material record.

Preconditions:

The actor is on Material List Screen.
The system has loaded the search controls.

Postconditions:

The filtered material list is displayed based on the entered search criteria.

Normal Flow:

The actor enters keyword into the Search Bar and/or selects filter criteria such as Status or Material Type.
The actor clicks the Search button.
The system validates the input criteria.
The system searches material records matching the criteria.
The system refreshes the material table with matching records.
The actor views the search result.

Alternative Flows:

A1. Actor resets the criteria

The actor clicks the Reset button.
The system clears all entered search/filter criteria.
The system reloads the default material list.

A2. No matching result found

In step 4, the system finds no matching record.
The system displays an empty list with "No material found."

Exception:

E1. Invalid input format

In step 3, the system detects invalid search input.
The system highlights the invalid field and displays with "Invalid search criteria."

Business Rule:

BR-04: Search keyword shall support partial matching on material code and material name.
BR-05: Search result shall only include records that match all selected filters.
UC-MAT-03_Open Material Detail

ID and Name
UC-MAT-03 – Open Material Detail

Primary Actor:
Authorized User

Secondary Actor:
Production Manager, Administrator

Description:
As an authorized user, I want to open a material detail screen from the material list so that I can review full material information.

Preconditions:

The actor is on Material List Screen.
At least one material record is displayed.

Postconditions:

The selected material’s detail is displayed on Material Detail Screen.

Normal Flow:

The actor locates a material record in the list.
The actor clicks on Material Code or View Detail action of the selected record.
The system opens Material Detail Screen for the selected material.
The system displays detailed information of that material.

Alternative Flows:

A1. Material record no longer exists

In step 3, the system cannot find the selected material record.
The system stays on Material List Screen and displays with "The selected material does not exist."

Exception:

E1. Actor has no permission to view detail

In step 2, the actor attempts to open a material detail without permission.
The system denies access and displays with "You do not have permission to access this function."

Business Rule:

BR-06: Only existing material records can be opened.
BR-07: Material detail access shall follow role-based authorization.
UC-MAT-04_Open Material Form

ID and Name
UC-MAT-04 – Open Material Form

Primary Actor:
Authorized User

Secondary Actor:
Administrator

Description:
As an authorized user, I want to navigate from the material list to the material form so that I can create a new material or edit an existing material.

Preconditions:

The actor is on Material List Screen.
The actor has create or update permission.

Postconditions:

Material Form Screen is opened in create mode or update mode.

Normal Flow:

The actor clicks Add New to create a new material, or clicks Edit on an existing material row.
The system checks the actor’s permission.
The system opens Material Form Screen.
If the actor selected Add New, the form is displayed in create mode.
If the actor selected Edit, the system loads the selected material data and displays the form in update mode.

Alternative Flows:

A1. Selected material is inactive but still editable by authorized actor

The actor clicks Edit on an inactive material.
The system allows opening the form if the actor has sufficient permission.
The form is displayed in update mode.

Exception:

E1. Actor has no create/update permission

In step 2, the system determines that the actor does not have proper permission.
The system does not open the form and displays with "You do not have permission to perform this action."

E2. Selected material no longer exists

In step 5, the system cannot load the selected material data.
The system remains on Material List Screen and displays with "The selected material does not exist."

Business Rule:

BR-08: Only users with create permission can access create mode.
BR-09: Only users with update permission can access update mode.
BR-10: Material Form Screen shall reuse one UI for both create and update actions.
2.1.x.x Material Detail Modal Pop-up
a. UI Specifications
Material Detail Modal

Brief Description
This modal displays detailed information of a selected material from the Material List Screen. It allows the authorized actor to view full material specifications and optionally perform actions such as edit, activate, or deactivate the material. The modal is opened as an overlay without navigating away from the current screen.

Mockup Screen
[Insert mockup of Material Detail Modal Pop-up here]

UI Components / Field Description / Requirements
No.	Component / Field	Type	Description	Requirements / Notes
1	Modal Title	Label	Display: Material Detail	Fixed text
2	Close Button (X)	Icon Button	Close modal	Always visible
3	Material Code	Text	Unique identifier of material	Read-only
4	Material Name	Text	Name of material	Read-only
5	Material Type	Text	Category/type of material	Optional
6	Unit	Text	Unit of measure	Example: sheet, kg
7	Standard Size	Text	Dimension/specification	Optional
8	Description	Text Area	Additional notes	Optional
9	Status	Badge	Show Active / Inactive	Color-coded
10	Created At	Text	Created date/time	Read-only
11	Updated At	Text	Last updated date/time	Read-only
12	Created By	Text	User who created material	Optional
13	Updated By	Text	Last updated user	Optional
14	Edit Button	Button	Open Material Form Screen in update mode	Visible with permission
15	Activate Button	Button	Activate material	Visible when status = Inactive
16	Deactivate Button	Button	Deactivate material	Visible when status = Active
17	Close Button	Button	Close modal	Same as X button
UI Requirements / Notes
The modal shall appear as an overlay on top of Material List Screen.
Background content shall be disabled while modal is open.
The modal shall be centered and responsive.
Only one modal instance can be opened at a time.
Status shall be visually distinguishable:
Active → green badge
Inactive → grey/red badge
Clicking outside modal or pressing ESC may close modal (optional).
Edit / Activate / Deactivate buttons shall be displayed based on user permission.
This modal is used for quick view, avoiding navigation to another screen.
