UC-MAT-05_View Material Detail (Modal)

ID and Name
UC-MAT-05 – View Material Detail (Modal)

Primary Actor:
Authorized User

Secondary Actor:
Production Manager, Administrator

Description:
As an authorized user, I want to view detailed information of a material in a modal so that I can quickly review its data without leaving the current screen.

Preconditions:

The actor is on Material List Screen
At least one material record exists

Postconditions:

Material detail modal is displayed
Actor can perform further actions or close modal

Normal Flow:

The actor clicks Material Code or View Detail icon on a material row.
The system retrieves material data.
The system opens Material Detail Modal Pop-up.
The system displays full material information.
The actor reviews the information.

Alternative Flows:

A1. Actor closes modal

The actor clicks Close button (X) or Close button.
The system closes the modal.
The actor returns to Material List Screen.

Exception:

E1. Material not found

In step 2, the system cannot find the material record.
The system displays message with "The selected material does not exist."
The modal is not opened.

E2. System error while loading data

In step 2, system error occurs.
The system displays with "Unable to load material details."

Business Rule:

BR-01: Only authorized users can view material details.
BR-02: Material information displayed must reflect the latest saved data.
BR-03: Modal shall not allow editing directly; editing must be done via Material Form Screen.
UC-MAT-06_Activate Material

ID and Name
UC-MAT-06 – Activate Material

Primary Actor:
Administrator

Secondary Actor:
None

Description:
As an administrator, I want to activate an inactive material so that it can be used in BOM and production.

Preconditions:

Material status = Inactive
Actor has permission

Postconditions:

Material status is updated to Active

Normal Flow:

The actor clicks Activate Button.
The system displays confirmation dialog with "Are you sure you want to activate this material?"
The actor confirms.
The system updates material status to Active.
The system updates UI and displays with "Material activated successfully."

Alternative Flows:

A1. Actor cancels action

At step 2, actor selects Cancel.
The system closes dialog.

Exception:

E1. Material already active

System detects status is already Active.
Display with "Material is already active."

Business Rule:

BR-04: Only Active materials can be used in BOM and production planning
UC-MAT-07_Deactivate Material

ID and Name
UC-MAT-07 – Deactivate Material

Primary Actor:
Administrator

Secondary Actor:
None

Description:
As an administrator, I want to deactivate a material so that it is no longer used in new BOM or production processes.

Preconditions:

Material status = Active
Actor has permission

Postconditions:

Material status is updated to Inactive

Normal Flow:

The actor clicks Deactivate Button.
The system displays confirmation dialog with "Are you sure you want to deactivate this material?"
The actor confirms.
The system updates status to Inactive.
The system updates UI and displays with "Material deactivated successfully."

Alternative Flows:

A1. Actor cancels action

At step 2, actor selects Cancel.
The system closes dialog.

Exception:

E1. Material is being used in active BOM

System detects dependency.
System blocks action and displays with "Material cannot be deactivated because it is used in active BOM."

Business Rule:

BR-05: Material used in active BOM cannot be deactivated
BR-06: Deactivated material must not be selectable in new transactions
